# Tiered Advanced RAG Upgrade — COMPLETE

Status: implemented and green (desktop suite 123 passed). Supersedes the
earlier Qwen2.5/Ollama migration plan in this file.

## What landed (core/ stack)

- RAG_LEVEL tiers: basic | standard (default) | full — core/config.py
- Hybrid retrieval: dense (bge-small) + BM25 keyword scoring fused with
  reciprocal rank fusion — core/bm25.py (new), core/vectorstore.py
- Query condensation for follow-ups: heuristic (standard) or one LLM call
  (full), graceful fallback — core/condense.py (new)
- Cross-encoder reranking: bge-reranker-base on CPU, auto-disabled below
  8GB RAM, broken-flag fallback — core/rerank.py (new)
- Contextual chunk enrichment: [From file — pages N] headers at ingestion —
  core/ingestion.py chunk_text_enriched()
- Wiring: build_context_block dispatches on tier; build_chat_messages gained
  retrieval_query kwarg; chat routers + server/orchestration.py condense
  before retrieval
- Security fixes from audit: engagement-scoped BM25 cache + where_pred,
  bounded marker regex, sanitized filenames in prompt headers, condense
  fallback logging, env parsing hardened (_env_int/_env_float)
- Tests: desktop/tests/test_rag_upgrade.py (18 offline tests) covering
  hybrid retrieval, cross-engagement isolation, tier gating, condensation,
  rerank fallback, enrichment, hostile-input performance

## Environment

- RAG_LEVEL=standard (basic|standard|full)
- RERANK_BACKEND=sentence-transformers ("none" disables)
- RERANK_MODEL / RERANK_CANDIDATE_MULTIPLIER / RERANK_MIN_RAM_GB / BM25_RRF_K

## Remaining follow-ups

- Legacy backend/app/ stack: mirror the RAG upgrade if the Docker/Open WebUI
  deployment is still needed
- Live smoke test of bge-reranker-base scoring (network-dependent)
